      {
        "id": 222722,
        "name": "jffdougan",
        "username": "jffdougan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/{size}/1882_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-01-25T01:20:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Paul\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/paul/48/5862_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Paul:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/anubis\">@Anubis</a></p>\n<p>The ability creation is much easier than Mutants and Masterminds. There are a ton of different pre-made options that you can mix and match and tweak to make more flavorful for your character. For a good example of this, watch the Character Creation episode of the livestream RPG that I ran, and see what Chris Burton does with his character. (That section will make more sense once you have the core rulebook in front of you).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It might be too much to handle, but - I propose that one of the KS updates take the form of a “play-by-post” CC session with 2-3 of the Playtesters who have not previously seen any iteration of the rules. I volunteer to be one, because I know exactly who I want to build. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
